.Dd November 18, 2026
.Dt EINKD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm einkd
.Nd RavenBSD E-Ink fetch/render/refresh service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/einkd
.Op --dry-run
.Op --once
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the fetch, render and full-refresh service core for the Pi 4 7.5-inch
UC8179 E-Ink panel.
The service is disabled by default in the release image
.Pq Va enable = false
and is ordered after
.Dq getty
and
.Dq netd ,
so it never runs on the boot or login path.
.Pp
The current binary supports the host-tested dry-run path:
.Bl -tag -width "--dry-run" -compact
.It Fl -dry-run
Use the static content source and a dry-run panel that only counts and logs
the rendered frame.
No SPI, GPIO, panel or network access is performed.
.It Fl -once
Perform one bounded fetch/render/refresh and exit 0.
.El
.Pp
A run without
.Fl -dry-run
exits with
.Dq hardware adapter not built
until E4 supplies the SPI/GPIO adapter.
The service manifest keeps
.Nm
disabled by default; the
.Dq einkd-supervision
qtest starts it after login and checks one dry-run refresh.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/services.d/einkd.toml" -compact
.It Pa /sbin/einkd
The service binary.
.It Pa /etc/services.d/einkd.toml
The disabled service manifest.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getty 1 ,
.Xr netd 8
